s count for T1: 3 left, so getting a third T1 for pung is possible. B3: 3 left. W3: 3 left.\\n\\nIf I discard B3, I keep T1 pair and W sequence. Then I have: W2, W3(2), W4, T1(2). That's 6 tiles. I need to form two melds and a pair from these 6. Possible: pair T1, chow W2,W3,W4 (uses W2, one W3, W4), leftover W3. Then I need one more meld from just one W3? Not possible. So I would need to draw tiles to complete.\\n\\nIf I discard T1, I keep B3 pair and W sequence. Then hand: W2, W3(2), W4, B3(2). That's 6 tiles. Possible: pair B3, chow W2,W3,W4 (uses W2, one W3, W4), leftover W3. Same issue: leftover single W3.\\n\\nIf I discard one W3, hand: W2, W3, W4, T1(2), B3(2). That's 6 tiles? Actually, discarding one W3 leaves: W2(1), W3(1), W4(1), T1(2), B3(2) = 1+1+1+2+2=7 tiles. Wait, originally 8 tiles, discard one becomes 7 hand tiles. Then I need to form two melds and a pair from 7 tiles, which is possible if one meld uses 3, pair uses 2, leftover 2 tiles need to form another meld? Actually, total needed: 2 more melds (6 tiles) + pair (2 tiles) = 8 tiles, but I have only 7 after discard, so I would need to draw one more tile to get to 8 hand tiles? Actually, after discard, I have 7 hand tiles, plus 6 in melds = 13 tiles total. Then I need one more tile to win, which would be drawn. So with 7 hand tiles, I can have: one meld (3 tiles), one pair (2 tiles), and two leftover tiles that need to form another meld (3 tiles) but I have only 2, so I need to draw to complete. So still incomplete.\\n\\nActually, the goal is to reach a ready hand where I need one tile to complete. So I should aim for a shape where 7 tiles can be arranged into one complete meld, one pair, and two tiles that are one away from a meld (e.g., two tiles that need a third to form chow or pung).\\n\\nSo after discard, I want my 7 hand tiles to be: one meld (3 tiles), one pair (2 tiles), and a partial meld of 2 tiles that need one tile to complete.\\n\\nFor example, if I discard T1, hand: W2, W3(2), W4, B3