m sequence.  \n\nAmong T4 and T2, T4 is slightly worse because T4 only 1 left in wall, while T2 has 2 left but T1 gone, T3 only 1 left. Actually both are bad, but T4 discard keeps your W2-W3-W4 possibility alive and B3 pair intact.  \n\nReason:  \nDiscarding T4 maintains two potential pairs (W3 and B3) and the W2-W3-W4 chow possibility. It also reduces clutter in the hand (already have T4 in a meld). T2 is also isolated but might be kept if hoping for T2-T3-T4, but T3 only 1 left and T4 already in meld, so less likely.  \n\nFinal choice: Play T4.  \n\nAnswer: Play T4"}
